# Welcome to Markdown Viewer 3.10.5

_Released October 27, 2026_

This release connects the desktop app safely to existing Markdown files and folders, adds direct control over Preview libraries and emoji appearance, and makes local recovery more dependable when saves, moves, imports, or external edits overlap.

Everything here ships with the web, PWA, Docker, and desktop editions unless a feature is explicitly marked desktop-only. **Happy coding!**

[View release on GitHub](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/releases/tag/v3.10.5) [Open the full changelog](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)

---

## Highlights

- **Work with existing files in the desktop app.** Link a Markdown file or folder without importing or moving it, keep automatic recovery drafts separate, and decide explicitly when to write an original.
- **Tune the Preview to your work.** Choose the code theme, math font, Mermaid theme and style, and supported emoji skin tone from one compact settings dialog.
- **Find emoji by meaning instead of alphabet.** Browse ten familiar groups, search names, aliases, keywords, or emoji, collect several choices, and copy or insert them in order.
- **Recover once, then continue normally.** A successfully saved recovered document now consumes only its matching journal, preventing the same recovery copy from returning on every launch.
- **Keep destructive operations coordinated.** Saves, deletes, moves, workspace replacement, linked scans, and Secret Workspace transitions preserve newer drafts and report partial or failed work accurately.

> [!TIP]
> In the desktop app, open the **Linked Workspace** menu and choose **Link file** or **Link folder**. Editing saves a recovery draft inside the Markdown Viewer vault; press **Ctrl+S** only when you want to update the external original.

## Link desktop files and folders without importing them

The new desktop-only **Linked Workspace** sits beside the managed Vault and Secret Workspace. Link one `.md` or `.markdown` file or scan a folder recursively while keeping each original at its existing path. Source paths appear on hover, nested folder structure is retained, linking progress is visible, and normalized path identity avoids accidental duplicate links, including Windows UNC paths.

Autosave writes a recovery draft under the app's separate Linked Workspace storage instead of changing the original. **Save / Ctrl+S** captures current Editor input, verifies the draft and source, and then writes explicitly. External changes, missing files, and conflicts keep the draft and ask what to do. **Save As…** creates another linked file, while **Convert to Workspace copy** preserves the current draft as an independent Vault document without changing its source.

Folder links support rescanning, sidebar-only grouping, removal that never deletes originals, drag conversion to Vault, and export of a Vault folder as a separate linked folder. Removed or converted paths stay excluded from automatic scans across overlapping roots but can return through an explicit rescan or relink. Browser and Docker builds hide native linking controls.

Scans are deliberately bounded by file size, staged content, entry, file, directory, depth, and time limits. Workspace backups can retain recoverable linked drafts, but imported paths are treated as data rather than permission: a restored draft must be linked again before it can write an external file. Recovery remains a safety net, not an independent backup.

## Customize Preview rendering

Open **Workspace settings → Preview Styling** to manage five saved preferences:

- **Code theme** for highlighted code blocks.
- **Math font** for MathJax output.
- **Diagram theme** and **Diagram style** for Mermaid.
- **Emoji skin tone** for supported unqualified shortcodes and picker artwork.

Changes apply automatically in normal and split Preview. Compact info buttons explain the Mermaid and emoji controls on hover, keyboard focus, or tap. **Reset defaults** changes only these preferences, not document content.

Math stays available in the bundled Computer Modern style while an optional font downloads. Shared downloads are reused, only the newest selection can update the renderer, and failed or superseded requests cannot strand MathJax or block Reset. Code-theme and font assets may still require the network, including in the desktop app.

## Browse a categorized emoji picker

**GitHub Emojis** now opens a compact grid grouped into smileys, people, nature, food, travel, activities, objects, symbols, flags, and GitHub extras. Search spans all groups using English names, aliases, keywords, or an emoji. Aliases share a tile, while an exact alias search preserves that shortcode.

Selections remain in an ordered tray while you search or change categories. Remove individual choices, copy the complete selection, or insert every shortcode in order. Arrow keys navigate categories and tiles, Space or Enter selects, Escape closes, and narrow layouts provide a swipeable category strip.

The picker shows clear catalog, tile-loading, failure, and retry states without briefly switching to a mismatched native emoji style. Images are requested only near visible rows and reused when revisited. The picker and selection tray follow live and saved skin-tone changes without clearing the search or selection; unsupported or unavailable artwork retains a usable fallback.

## Stronger recovery and storage safety

Normal saves now retain newer content or comment journals that arrive while an older write is completing. Successful saves of recovered copies track and consume only the exact source journal they committed, so reopened recovery documents do not multiply indefinitely. Failed saves, metadata-only saves, and newer replacement records remain recoverable.

Document deletion coordinates with queued writes, desktop moves reject occupied destinations, case-only Vault renames remain possible, and workspace reset or backup restore blocks new editing while pending operations settle. Folder registration, linked exclusions, source refresh, Save As watchers, and conversion commits use durable metadata before reporting success. Moving a Vault document to Secret Workspace preserves the encrypted record before plaintext cleanup.

Chooser focus is also safer: delayed reference, media, and table dialogs no longer redirect typing after the originating document or selection changes. Review recovery keeps newer replies instead of restoring stale comment metadata.

## Interface, startup, and authoring polish

Preview and Explorer now use matching startup placeholders. The slash-command menu shares the app's compact dropdown styling, stays clear of the typing line, completes chooser-based commands, preserves the correct upload target, and aligns primary and secondary Editors. Split documents use consistent spacing and empty-state hints, and inactive panes no longer receive a misleading focus border.

The Linked Workspace guide opens in Split view with concise steps and diagrams. Explorer actions distinguish linking from Trash, header context menus stay disabled, plain file icons keep managed documents visually quiet, and workspace expansion colors remain consistent.

## Quality, localization, and distribution

All 15 locale catalogs include the Linked Workspace, Preview Styling, emoji, recovery, and v3.10.5 release-note labels with matching placeholders. Web, service-worker, Docker, and Neutralino resources include the new stores, adapters, native-source bridge, emoji catalog, icons, styles, and tests. DOMPurify and YAML dependencies include their current security fixes for this release line.

Coverage now includes linked file/folder workflows, scan boundaries and races, source conflicts, Save As watchers, conversion and removal failures, backup trust boundaries, recovered-journal cleanup, desktop filesystem moves, Preview Styling lifecycle, MathJax resources, syntax themes, emoji categories and lazy loading, startup placeholders, slash commands, localization, and web/desktop isolation.

